{
  "video": {
    "id": "qY0ixUWJx0g",
    "title": "Pedigrees | MIT 7.01SC Fundamentals of Biology",
    "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qY0ixUWJx0g",
    "channel": "MIT OpenCourseWare",
    "duration": 713,
    "language": "en"
  },
  "segment_count": 169,
  "segments": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "start": 7.32,
      "end": 8.53,
      "duration": 1.21,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: Hello and welcome to the"
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "start": 8.53,
      "end": 10.66,
      "duration": 2.13,
      "text": "help session on pedigrees."
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "start": 10.66,
      "end": 13.56,
      "duration": 2.9,
      "text": "Today, we will be working out a problem together."
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "start": 13.56,
      "end": 17.05,
      "duration": 3.49,
      "text": "If you have not yet had a chance to work it on your own,"
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "start": 17.05,
      "end": 19.6,
      "duration": 2.55,
      "text": "please do so now, and return to this video"
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "start": 19.6,
      "end": 20.85,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "when you are done."
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "start": 29.39,
      "end": 32.38,
      "duration": 2.99,
      "text": "Now that you've had a chance to look at this problem, let's"
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "start": 32.38,
      "end": 33.78,
      "duration": 1.4,
      "text": "work it out together."
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "start": 33.78,
      "end": 36.78,
      "duration": 3.0,
      "text": "The first part of this question asks, what is the"
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "start": 36.78,
      "end": 40.93,
      "duration": 4.15,
      "text": "mode of inheritance that is observed in this pedigree?"
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "start": 40.93,
      "end": 43.73,
      "duration": 2.8,
      "text": "So, we know that there are two main types of modes of"
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "start": 43.73,
      "end": 44.8,
      "duration": 1.07,
      "text": "inheritance."
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "start": 44.8,
      "end": 47.78,
      "duration": 2.98,
      "text": "It can either be dominant or recessive."
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "start": 47.78,
      "end": 51.03,
      "duration": 3.25,
      "text": "And from there it can either be autosomal or X-linked."
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "start": 53.77,
      "end": 57.72,
      "duration": 3.95,
      "text": "If a disease follows a dominant inheritance pattern,"
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "start": 57.72,
      "end": 60.99,
      "duration": 3.27,
      "text": "generally, it must be present in every generation."
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "start": 60.99,
      "end": 64.23,
      "duration": 3.24,
      "text": "So here we notice that the disease is present in the"
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "start": 64.23,
      "end": 67.66,
      "duration": 3.43,
      "text": "first generation, but it's not present in anyone in the"
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "start": 67.66,
      "end": 69.43,
      "duration": 1.77,
      "text": "second generation."
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "start": 69.43,
      "end": 73.5,
      "duration": 4.07,
      "text": "However, then it reappears in the third generation."
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "start": 73.5,
      "end": 77.17,
      "duration": 3.67,
      "text": "This suggests that the disease is recessive."
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "start": 87.54,
      "end": 90.95,
      "duration": 3.41,
      "text": "So now, do we think this disease is"
    },
    {
      "index": 22,
      "start": 90.95,
      "end": 93.91,
      "duration": 2.96,
      "text": "autosomal or is it X-linked?"
    },
    {
      "index": 23,
      "start": 93.91,
      "end": 97.01,
      "duration": 3.1,
      "text": "So we look at the pedigree again, and upon closer"
    },
    {
      "index": 24,
      "start": 97.01,
      "end": 101.0,
      "duration": 3.99,
      "text": "inspection, we notice that the affected"
    },
    {
      "index": 25,
      "start": 101.0,
      "end": 104.04,
      "duration": 3.04,
      "text": "individuals are only males."
    },
    {
      "index": 26,
      "start": 104.04,
      "end": 106.62,
      "duration": 2.58,
      "text": "This is a key characteristic of an"
    },
    {
      "index": 27,
      "start": 106.62,
      "end": 109.37,
      "duration": 2.75,
      "text": "X-linked recessive disease."
    },
    {
      "index": 28,
      "start": 109.37,
      "end": 112.99,
      "duration": 3.62,
      "text": "However, we're also given more information that tells us that"
    },
    {
      "index": 29,
      "start": 112.99,
      "end": 116.46,
      "duration": 3.47,
      "text": "this individual here does not carry an allele associated"
    },
    {
      "index": 30,
      "start": 116.46,
      "end": 119.37,
      "duration": 2.91,
      "text": "with the affected phenotype."
    },
    {
      "index": 31,
      "start": 119.37,
      "end": 124.1,
      "duration": 4.73,
      "text": "This rules out the possibility that this disease could be an"
    },
    {
      "index": 32,
      "start": 124.1,
      "end": 126.45,
      "duration": 2.35,
      "text": "autosomal recessive disease."
    },
    {
      "index": 33,
      "start": 126.45,
      "end": 127.89,
      "duration": 1.44,
      "text": "Thus, the most likely mode of"
    },
    {
      "index": 34,
      "start": 127.89,
      "end": 129.795,
      "duration": 1.905,
      "text": "inheritance is X-linked recessive."
    },
    {
      "index": 35,
      "start": 137.63,
      "end": 141.4,
      "duration": 3.77,
      "text": "Great, so moving on to the second part of this problem,"
    },
    {
      "index": 36,
      "start": 141.4,
      "end": 144.48,
      "duration": 3.08,
      "text": "we are asked to determine the genotypes of individuals"
    },
    {
      "index": 37,
      "start": 144.48,
      "end": 147.28,
      "duration": 2.8,
      "text": "number one and number three."
    },
    {
      "index": 38,
      "start": 147.28,
      "end": 151.94,
      "duration": 4.66,
      "text": "So, if we look at this pedigree, we know individual"
    },
    {
      "index": 39,
      "start": 151.94,
      "end": 157.4,
      "duration": 5.46,
      "text": "one is female and not affected by the disease."
    },
    {
      "index": 40,
      "start": 157.4,
      "end": 164.86,
      "duration": 7.46,
      "text": "Female individuals contain two X chromosomes, and since she"
    },
    {
      "index": 41,
      "start": 164.86,
      "end": 170.345,
      "duration": 5.485,
      "text": "is not affected she must contain at least one large R."
    },
    {
      "index": 42,
      "start": 170.345,
      "end": 173.17,
      "duration": 2.825,
      "text": "So we'll call the allele associated with the"
    },
    {
      "index": 43,
      "start": 173.17,
      "end": 174.42,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "disease small r."
    },
    {
      "index": 44,
      "start": 179.85,
      "end": 183.95,
      "duration": 4.1,
      "text": "We do not yet know what her second X chromosome could be."
    },
    {
      "index": 45,
      "start": 183.95,
      "end": 189.05,
      "duration": 5.1,
      "text": "It could be either another large R or it"
    },
    {
      "index": 46,
      "start": 189.05,
      "end": 190.1,
      "duration": 1.05,
      "text": "could be a small r."
    },
    {
      "index": 47,
      "start": 190.1,
      "end": 193.14,
      "duration": 3.04,
      "text": "And she also would still not be affected by the disease."
    },
    {
      "index": 48,
      "start": 201.23,
      "end": 203.93,
      "duration": 2.7,
      "text": "This male right here is affected by the disease."
    },
    {
      "index": 49,
      "start": 203.93,
      "end": 206.41,
      "duration": 2.48,
      "text": "So he must have an X with a small r."
    },
    {
      "index": 50,
      "start": 210.48,
      "end": 213.32,
      "duration": 2.84,
      "text": "Remember that males have one X chromosome and one Y"
    },
    {
      "index": 51,
      "start": 213.32,
      "end": 215.65,
      "duration": 2.33,
      "text": "chromosome."
    },
    {
      "index": 52,
      "start": 215.65,
      "end": 219.25,
      "duration": 3.6,
      "text": "So now, making our way down to individual number three."
    },
    {
      "index": 53,
      "start": 219.25,
      "end": 223.12,
      "duration": 3.87,
      "text": "Individual number three does not have the disease and is"
    },
    {
      "index": 54,
      "start": 223.12,
      "end": 225.52,
      "duration": 2.4,
      "text": "female, so again, must have two X chromosomes."
    },
    {
      "index": 55,
      "start": 231.27,
      "end": 234.06,
      "duration": 2.79,
      "text": "One of the X chromosomes must come from her father and the"
    },
    {
      "index": 56,
      "start": 234.06,
      "end": 235.94,
      "duration": 1.88,
      "text": "other from her mother."
    },
    {
      "index": 57,
      "start": 235.94,
      "end": 239.07,
      "duration": 3.13,
      "text": "The only X chromosome that her father can pass along to her"
    },
    {
      "index": 58,
      "start": 239.07,
      "end": 242.94,
      "duration": 3.87,
      "text": "is X small r."
    },
    {
      "index": 59,
      "start": 242.94,
      "end": 245.93,
      "duration": 2.99,
      "text": "In order for her to not be affected with the disease, her"
    },
    {
      "index": 60,
      "start": 245.93,
      "end": 253.48,
      "duration": 7.55,
      "text": "other X chromosome must have a large R."
    },
    {
      "index": 61,
      "start": 253.48,
      "end": 256.86,
      "duration": 3.38,
      "text": "She was able to get this genotype with her mother"
    },
    {
      "index": 62,
      "start": 256.86,
      "end": 260.42,
      "duration": 3.56,
      "text": "having either of these two genotypes."
    },
    {
      "index": 63,
      "start": 260.42,
      "end": 262.78,
      "duration": 2.36,
      "text": "To make sure that both of these genotypes are possible"
    },
    {
      "index": 64,
      "start": 262.78,
      "end": 267.32,
      "duration": 4.54,
      "text": "for this mother, we need to examine her other children."
    },
    {
      "index": 65,
      "start": 267.32,
      "end": 269.3,
      "duration": 1.98,
      "text": "Her son here is unaffected."
    },
    {
      "index": 66,
      "start": 269.3,
      "end": 279.54,
      "duration": 10.24,
      "text": "So his genotype must have been X large R, Y. It's possible"
    },
    {
      "index": 67,
      "start": 279.54,
      "end": 282.64,
      "duration": 3.1,
      "text": "for him to get this genotype when the mother has either of"
    },
    {
      "index": 68,
      "start": 282.64,
      "end": 285.56,
      "duration": 2.92,
      "text": "these two genotypes."
    },
    {
      "index": 69,
      "start": 285.56,
      "end": 289.635,
      "duration": 4.075,
      "text": "Similarly, this daughter could be unaffected just as this"
    },
    {
      "index": 70,
      "start": 289.635,
      "end": 291.0,
      "duration": 1.365,
      "text": "daughter was unaffected."
    },
    {
      "index": 71,
      "start": 291.0,
      "end": 293.97,
      "duration": 2.97,
      "text": "So the mother can have either of these two genotypes."
    },
    {
      "index": 72,
      "start": 293.97,
      "end": 296.77,
      "duration": 2.8,
      "text": "And we're unable to rule out one of them."
    },
    {
      "index": 73,
      "start": 296.77,
      "end": 299.62,
      "duration": 2.85,
      "text": "So let me just write up the answer over here."
    },
    {
      "index": 74,
      "start": 319.02,
      "end": 321.03,
      "duration": 2.01,
      "text": "All right, so far, so good."
    },
    {
      "index": 75,
      "start": 321.03,
      "end": 324.06,
      "duration": 3.03,
      "text": "Next, we're asked to calculate the probability that"
    },
    {
      "index": 76,
      "start": 324.06,
      "end": 327.72,
      "duration": 3.66,
      "text": "individual A is affected."
    },
    {
      "index": 77,
      "start": 327.72,
      "end": 332.96,
      "duration": 5.24,
      "text": "Individual A is over here at the bottom of the pedigree."
    },
    {
      "index": 78,
      "start": 332.96,
      "end": 337.52,
      "duration": 4.56,
      "text": "In order for individual A to be affected, she must have the"
    },
    {
      "index": 79,
      "start": 337.52,
      "end": 338.77,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "following genotype."
    },
    {
      "index": 80,
      "start": 345.38,
      "end": 348.46,
      "duration": 3.08,
      "text": "The only way for her to get two little r's is for her to"
    },
    {
      "index": 81,
      "start": 348.46,
      "end": 351.1,
      "duration": 2.64,
      "text": "get one from her father and one from her mother."
    },
    {
      "index": 82,
      "start": 351.1,
      "end": 353.97,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "We know this is possible because her father is affected"
    },
    {
      "index": 83,
      "start": 353.97,
      "end": 359.97,
      "duration": 6.0,
      "text": "with the following genotype of Y, X small r."
    },
    {
      "index": 84,
      "start": 359.97,
      "end": 361.79,
      "duration": 1.82,
      "text": "Her mother is not affected."
    },
    {
      "index": 85,
      "start": 361.79,
      "end": 365.84,
      "duration": 4.05,
      "text": "So for her to get this small r, her mother must be a"
    },
    {
      "index": 86,
      "start": 365.84,
      "end": 370.1,
      "duration": 4.26,
      "text": "carrier for the disease, and have the genotype X"
    },
    {
      "index": 87,
      "start": 370.1,
      "end": 374.86,
      "duration": 4.76,
      "text": "large R, X small r."
    },
    {
      "index": 88,
      "start": 374.86,
      "end": 379.94,
      "duration": 5.08,
      "text": "So in order to determine the probability that A is affected"
    },
    {
      "index": 89,
      "start": 379.94,
      "end": 383.85,
      "duration": 3.91,
      "text": "with both X small r's, we must also know the probability that"
    },
    {
      "index": 90,
      "start": 383.85,
      "end": 386.57,
      "duration": 2.72,
      "text": "her mother was a carrier for the disease."
    },
    {
      "index": 91,
      "start": 386.57,
      "end": 390.19,
      "duration": 3.62,
      "text": "Let's call her mother individual C."
    },
    {
      "index": 92,
      "start": 390.19,
      "end": 393.82,
      "duration": 3.63,
      "text": "So, we know the genotypes of her parents."
    },
    {
      "index": 93,
      "start": 393.82,
      "end": 395.41,
      "duration": 1.59,
      "text": "Her mother was a carrier."
    },
    {
      "index": 94,
      "start": 395.41,
      "end": 398.19,
      "duration": 2.78,
      "text": "And her father did not have the disease, so his genotype"
    },
    {
      "index": 95,
      "start": 398.19,
      "end": 405.42,
      "duration": 7.23,
      "text": "was Y with X large R. So to calculate the probability that"
    },
    {
      "index": 96,
      "start": 405.42,
      "end": 408.68,
      "duration": 3.26,
      "text": "individual C is a carrier for the disease, let's go back"
    },
    {
      "index": 97,
      "start": 408.68,
      "end": 410.731,
      "duration": 2.051,
      "text": "over here and draw out a Punnett square."
    },
    {
      "index": 98,
      "start": 420.24,
      "end": 422.41,
      "duration": 2.17,
      "text": "On one side, we're going to write the genotype of her"
    },
    {
      "index": 99,
      "start": 422.41,
      "end": 429.08,
      "duration": 6.67,
      "text": "father, which was Y because he's a male."
    },
    {
      "index": 100,
      "start": 429.08,
      "end": 433.21,
      "duration": 4.13,
      "text": "And then, he was not affected by the disease, so it was X"
    },
    {
      "index": 101,
      "start": 433.21,
      "end": 439.41,
      "duration": 6.2,
      "text": "with a large R. Her mother was a carrier."
    },
    {
      "index": 102,
      "start": 439.41,
      "end": 444.33,
      "duration": 4.92,
      "text": "So she had one copy that was X large R, and one copy that was"
    },
    {
      "index": 103,
      "start": 444.33,
      "end": 446.77,
      "duration": 2.44,
      "text": "x little r."
    },
    {
      "index": 104,
      "start": 446.77,
      "end": 450.63,
      "duration": 3.86,
      "text": "So next, we want to know the probability"
    },
    {
      "index": 105,
      "start": 450.63,
      "end": 453.27,
      "duration": 2.64,
      "text": "that she was a carrier."
    },
    {
      "index": 106,
      "start": 453.27,
      "end": 455.99,
      "duration": 2.72,
      "text": "The only ways you can get females is by looking at this"
    },
    {
      "index": 107,
      "start": 455.99,
      "end": 457.24,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "top row here."
    },
    {
      "index": 108,
      "start": 464.19,
      "end": 467.17,
      "duration": 2.98,
      "text": "So, for now, we're going to ignore the bottom row."
    },
    {
      "index": 109,
      "start": 467.17,
      "end": 471.09,
      "duration": 3.92,
      "text": "Of the two possible ways to generate a female, only one of"
    },
    {
      "index": 110,
      "start": 471.09,
      "end": 472.96,
      "duration": 1.87,
      "text": "them is a carrier."
    },
    {
      "index": 111,
      "start": 472.96,
      "end": 477.26,
      "duration": 4.3,
      "text": "So there's a 50% chance that a female will be a carrier."
    },
    {
      "index": 112,
      "start": 485.68,
      "end": 489.66,
      "duration": 3.98,
      "text": "So this is a 50% chance that individual C is a carrier,"
    },
    {
      "index": 113,
      "start": 489.66,
      "end": 494.33,
      "duration": 4.67,
      "text": "which we will denote with this half filled in circle."
    },
    {
      "index": 114,
      "start": 494.33,
      "end": 497.53,
      "duration": 3.2,
      "text": "All right, so now that we know the probability that C was a"
    },
    {
      "index": 115,
      "start": 497.53,
      "end": 500.61,
      "duration": 3.08,
      "text": "carrier, we need to know the probability that her progeny,"
    },
    {
      "index": 116,
      "start": 500.61,
      "end": 503.29,
      "duration": 2.68,
      "text": "A, was affected with the disease."
    },
    {
      "index": 117,
      "start": 503.29,
      "end": 508.57,
      "duration": 5.28,
      "text": "Again, looking back over here, her progeny needs to inherit"
    },
    {
      "index": 118,
      "start": 508.57,
      "end": 511.03,
      "duration": 2.46,
      "text": "the X small r from the mother and the X"
    },
    {
      "index": 119,
      "start": 511.03,
      "end": 513.15,
      "duration": 2.12,
      "text": "small r from the father."
    },
    {
      "index": 120,
      "start": 513.15,
      "end": 516.13,
      "duration": 2.98,
      "text": "So, once again, we can draw a Punnett square to better"
    },
    {
      "index": 121,
      "start": 516.13,
      "end": 517.38,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "understand this."
    },
    {
      "index": 122,
      "start": 526.84,
      "end": 529.7,
      "duration": 2.86,
      "text": "Individual A's father was indeed"
    },
    {
      "index": 123,
      "start": 529.7,
      "end": 531.34,
      "duration": 1.64,
      "text": "affected by the disease."
    },
    {
      "index": 124,
      "start": 531.34,
      "end": 536.96,
      "duration": 5.62,
      "text": "So his genotype was X small r and Y. Her mother, we just"
    },
    {
      "index": 125,
      "start": 536.96,
      "end": 541.73,
      "duration": 4.77,
      "text": "calculated the probability of her being a carrier, so she is"
    },
    {
      "index": 126,
      "start": 541.73,
      "end": 544.69,
      "duration": 2.96,
      "text": "X large R, X small r."
    },
    {
      "index": 127,
      "start": 547.5,
      "end": 550.55,
      "duration": 3.05,
      "text": "Now, we're looking at individual A, who is a female,"
    },
    {
      "index": 128,
      "start": 550.55,
      "end": 552.5,
      "duration": 1.95,
      "text": "so again, we can ignore the bottom row because"
    },
    {
      "index": 129,
      "start": 552.5,
      "end": 554.76,
      "duration": 2.26,
      "text": "this will be males."
    },
    {
      "index": 130,
      "start": 554.76,
      "end": 556.655,
      "duration": 1.895,
      "text": "Here are the progeny which are female."
    },
    {
      "index": 131,
      "start": 562.56,
      "end": 567.15,
      "duration": 4.59,
      "text": "Of the two possibilities, only the one on the right, X small"
    },
    {
      "index": 132,
      "start": 567.15,
      "end": 570.9,
      "duration": 3.75,
      "text": "r, X small r is affected by the disease."
    },
    {
      "index": 133,
      "start": 570.9,
      "end": 575.13,
      "duration": 4.23,
      "text": "So there is a 50% chance that A will be affected by the"
    },
    {
      "index": 134,
      "start": 575.13,
      "end": 578.22,
      "duration": 3.09,
      "text": "disease given that her mother is a carrier of the disease."
    },
    {
      "index": 135,
      "start": 583.95,
      "end": 588.33,
      "duration": 4.38,
      "text": "Now to finish up this part of the problem, we need to"
    },
    {
      "index": 136,
      "start": 588.33,
      "end": 590.76,
      "duration": 2.43,
      "text": "multiply these two probabilities together because"
    },
    {
      "index": 137,
      "start": 590.76,
      "end": 593.28,
      "duration": 2.52,
      "text": "we're looking at the probability that C is a"
    },
    {
      "index": 138,
      "start": 593.28,
      "end": 600.93,
      "duration": 7.65,
      "text": "carrier, and the probability that A is"
    },
    {
      "index": 139,
      "start": 600.93,
      "end": 602.18,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "affected with the disease."
    },
    {
      "index": 140,
      "start": 607.4,
      "end": 611.17,
      "duration": 3.77,
      "text": "This gives us our answer of one fourth."
    },
    {
      "index": 141,
      "start": 611.17,
      "end": 614.31,
      "duration": 3.14,
      "text": "All right, so, moving on to the last part of the problem."
    },
    {
      "index": 142,
      "start": 614.31,
      "end": 617.59,
      "duration": 3.28,
      "text": "We need to calculate the probability that B is affected"
    },
    {
      "index": 143,
      "start": 617.59,
      "end": 618.91,
      "duration": 1.32,
      "text": "with the disease."
    },
    {
      "index": 144,
      "start": 618.91,
      "end": 621.84,
      "duration": 2.93,
      "text": "So this isn't that hard now that we've drawn out all of"
    },
    {
      "index": 145,
      "start": 621.84,
      "end": 623.82,
      "duration": 1.98,
      "text": "these Punnett squares already."
    },
    {
      "index": 146,
      "start": 623.82,
      "end": 629.7,
      "duration": 5.88,
      "text": "So, let's take a look back at our pedigree over here."
    },
    {
      "index": 147,
      "start": 629.7,
      "end": 633.52,
      "duration": 3.82,
      "text": "If B is going to be affected with the disease, he must have"
    },
    {
      "index": 148,
      "start": 633.52,
      "end": 638.76,
      "duration": 5.24,
      "text": "the genotype Y, X with a small r."
    },
    {
      "index": 149,
      "start": 638.76,
      "end": 643.45,
      "duration": 4.69,
      "text": "He gets the Y from his father and he must get this X with a"
    },
    {
      "index": 150,
      "start": 643.45,
      "end": 645.77,
      "duration": 2.32,
      "text": "small r from his mother."
    },
    {
      "index": 151,
      "start": 645.77,
      "end": 649.6,
      "duration": 3.83,
      "text": "So again, we need the mother, C, to be a carrier."
    },
    {
      "index": 152,
      "start": 649.6,
      "end": 654.0,
      "duration": 4.4,
      "text": "So let's go back to our Punnett squares over here."
    },
    {
      "index": 153,
      "start": 654.0,
      "end": 656.51,
      "duration": 2.51,
      "text": "We know that there is a 50% chance that"
    },
    {
      "index": 154,
      "start": 656.51,
      "end": 659.31,
      "duration": 2.8,
      "text": "individual C is a carrier."
    },
    {
      "index": 155,
      "start": 659.31,
      "end": 663.22,
      "duration": 3.91,
      "text": "Now we need to look at individual B being affected by"
    },
    {
      "index": 156,
      "start": 663.22,
      "end": 663.81,
      "duration": 0.59,
      "text": "the disease."
    },
    {
      "index": 157,
      "start": 663.81,
      "end": 666.09,
      "duration": 2.28,
      "text": "So we can go ahead and fill in the bottom part of this"
    },
    {
      "index": 158,
      "start": 666.09,
      "end": 667.34,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "Punnett square."
    },
    {
      "index": 159,
      "start": 674.01,
      "end": 678.91,
      "duration": 4.9,
      "text": "So of these two males, that are possible, only one of them"
    },
    {
      "index": 160,
      "start": 678.91,
      "end": 680.62,
      "duration": 1.71,
      "text": "is affected with the disease."
    },
    {
      "index": 161,
      "start": 680.62,
      "end": 684.51,
      "duration": 3.89,
      "text": "So again, there is a 50% probability that that child"
    },
    {
      "index": 162,
      "start": 684.51,
      "end": 685.76,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "will be affected with the disease."
    },
    {
      "index": 163,
      "start": 690.56,
      "end": 692.34,
      "duration": 1.78,
      "text": "Again, we are going to multiply these"
    },
    {
      "index": 164,
      "start": 692.34,
      "end": 693.62,
      "duration": 1.28,
      "text": "probabilities together."
    },
    {
      "index": 165,
      "start": 693.62,
      "end": 698.27,
      "duration": 4.65,
      "text": "So the probability that the mother is a carrier, and that"
    },
    {
      "index": 166,
      "start": 698.27,
      "end": 706.47,
      "duration": 8.2,
      "text": "the son is affected with the disease, gives us one quarter."
    },
    {
      "index": 167,
      "start": 706.47,
      "end": 709.27,
      "duration": 2.8,
      "text": "That concludes our problem on pedigrees."
    },
    {
      "index": 168,
      "start": 709.27,
      "end": 710.52,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "Thank you for joining us."
    }
  ],
